<title>FINLAND: ESPOON SAHKO SAYS HAS 17 PCT OF INTERKRAFT.</title>
<headline>ESPOON SAHKO SAYS HAS 17 PCT OF INTERKRAFT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish energy group Espoon Sahko said in a statement on Tuesday it had acquired 16.7 percent of the shares in Norwegian Interkraft Trading ASA.</p>
<p>&quot;Based on a letter of intent between Espoon Sahko and Norwegian Soerkraft AS, Espoon Sahko has made a subscription on June 16, 1997, in a targeted share issue, after which it owns 1/6 of Interkraft Trading ASA's share capital,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Intekraft Trading is an electricity trading company operating on the Nordic electricity markets, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0240, news@Reuters.fi</p>
